     1,
     "Nö <br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\"> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mirt-p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; schrieb am So., 7. März 2021, 09:44:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #d3d3d3;max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000\">\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:10px 20px\">\r\n    <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"width:70%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:#333333\">\r\n              <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/mirt-package/topics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:#333333\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/mirt-package/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw114gn_N73DBZ4YrEDalxMk\">\r\n              mirt-p...@googlegroups.com</a>\r\n            </span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"text-align:right;width:30%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:20px/24px arial\"><a style=\"color:#dd4b39;text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw22sTKGqITZpzYhVsvcdQFb\">Google Groups</a></span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"width:32px\">\r\n            <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw22sTKGqITZpzYhVsvcdQFb\"><img style=\"border:0;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n          </td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:#f5f5f5\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial;color:#222222;padding:0px\">\r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n  \r\n  \r\n    Topic digest\r\n  \r\n  </a><br>\r\n  <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/mirt-package/topics\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/mirt-package/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw114gn_N73DBZ4YrEDalxMk\">View all topics</a>\r\n  </span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:#222222;padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n  <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_0\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      Nominal response model output?</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_1\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      multigroup anchor item specification</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_2\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      MIRT with small sample size but valid models</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_3\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      Multidimensional IRT: Negative slopes</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_4\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      CONSTRAINB + multipleGroup</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_5\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      IRT with covariates</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_6\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      EAP score estimation for multiple groups</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_7\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      Using MIRT results for SEM</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_0\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/d130a62523026a9b?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/d130a62523026a9b?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0tHjwkeGpbbPZ82DNXoj_d\">\r\n      Nominal response model output?\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 08:30PM -0500\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        I can take a look at some point, but am quite burdened with teaching and<br>\r\nother admin work while the term is still running. I&#39;ll start having more<br>\r\ntime for research/outside interests when this semester ends. Sorry for the<br>\r\ndelayed replies.<br>\r\nPhil<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_1\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/c88aa37c73a49847?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/c88aa37c73a49847?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3_DVN4JNhz_uQAfsP9yH_H\">\r\n      multigroup anchor item specification\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 08:26PM -0500\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        On Wed, Feb 17, 2021 at 11:01 AM Monika Vaheoja &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>monika...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\nwrote:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; A nice article about this aspect is &quot;Eggen, T. J. H. M., &amp; Verhelst, N.<br>\r\n&gt; D. (2011). Item calibration in incomplete testing designs. Psicologica,<br>\r\n&gt; 32(1), 107-132&quot;.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nI&#39;m not familiar with this paper, so I&#39;ll have to read it during some spare<br>\r\ntime. Thanks for the reference.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; estimating them seperaterly for each group? What method do you use when the<br>\r\n&gt; parameter slopes and intercepts are fixed? I cant find any exact literature<br>\r\n&gt; about it, unfortunatelly.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nI don&#39;t follow, multipleGroup() doesn&#39;t estimate the parameters separately,<br>\r\nit does so concurrently based on the complete log-likelihood function<br>\r\nsummed across the groups. That allows for equality constraints and such, as<br>\r\nwell as likelihood/Baysian inferences.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; matrix? I&#39;m interested in the observed information matrix from Mirt from<br>\r\n&gt; multigroup function, do you have any suggestions how could i obtain that<br>\r\n&gt; matrix directly?<br>\r\n <br>\r\nThe Oakes method is for the observed information. If you want the direct<br>\r\ninformation component just invert the ACOV estimate using<br>\r\n <br>\r\nOinfo &lt;- solve(vcov(yourMGmodel))).<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_2\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/1803610886530dd5?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/1803610886530dd5?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15aCPsTfepkKEgisryoDh_\">\r\n      MIRT with small sample size but valid models\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 08:17PM -0500\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        On Fri, Feb 19, 2021 at 4:34 AM Martin Lacher &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>lacher...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\nwrote:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; Hi there,<br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; I &quot;boldly&quot; did IRT analysis (mostly unidimensional GRM) on data with a<br>\r\n&gt; sample size of around N=100.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nDid you get *bold* results to, or just *italicized*? ;-P<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; After some model and item wrangling I got valid models (RMSEA around 0.5,<br>\r\n&gt; CFI and TLI &gt; 0.93, sometimes even 0.97, even Chi2 was ok).<br>\r\n <br>\r\nData reliability (empirical) rxx is &gt; 0.7.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nThere&#39;s a good amount of sampling variability in each of these estimates,<br>\r\nso proceed with caution. It&#39;s possible to bootstrap these estimates, though<br>\r\ngiven the sample size that&#39;s likely not a great idea, and the n.s. chi2<br>\r\nshouldn&#39;t be surprising given the limited information available in the<br>\r\nmoments (likely underpowered).<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; I wanted to use GRM in the first place to analyse the validity of the item<br>\r\n&gt; levels, which indeed gave me a lot of information about my code system, but<br>\r\n&gt; now I&#39;m concerned about the calculated factor scores.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nThere will no doubt be a good amount of bias and sampling variability given<br>\r\non 100 responses, and unless your test is very long there probably won&#39;t be<br>\r\nsufficient response data available to compensate either. So it&#39;s hard to<br>\r\nsay if your particular sample is good or not, including the quality of the<br>\r\nfactor scores. You could of course try a simulation study yourself to see<br>\r\njust how variable these parameters tend to be.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nPhil<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_3\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/b1de939475c20174?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/b1de939475c20174?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ef4TvNqmzpJu9IZSoD7AL\">\r\n      Multidimensional IRT: Negative slopes\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 08:10PM -0500\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Is the model you fit an exploratory or confirmatory factor analysis model?<br>\r\nIf the former this is quite common due to the rotational indeterminacy, and<br>\r\nyou could just multiply each axis by -1 to flip the signs for each<br>\r\ndimension. If the latter, this would be more unusual given the starting<br>\r\nvalues of mirt, but the same principle would apply. All latent variable<br>\r\nmodels are effectively sign indeterminate if the identification isn&#39;t based<br>\r\non some anchoring item, and in IRT models we often use the default 0 mean 1<br>\r\nvariance scaling, so this can crop up. HTH.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nPhil<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_4\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/455acf08965323d2?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/455acf08965323d2?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lC9Eo65Iam3_mQ6ajfSUZ\">\r\n      CONSTRAINB + multipleGroup\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 08:05PM -0500\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Assuming your group names are G1, G2, and G3 in the group factor:<br>\r\n <br>\r\nmodel &lt;- &quot;<br>\r\nF[G1] = 1-22<br>\r\nF[G1, G2] = 23-30<br>\r\nF[G2] = 1-42<br>\r\nF[G2, G3] = 43-52<br>\r\nF[G3] =  53-72&quot;<br>\r\n <br>\r\nSo pretty much a copy-paste of your initial specification. HTH.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nPhil<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\nOn Tue, Mar 2, 2021 at 2:09 PM Caio Lucidius Naberezny Azevedo &lt;<br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_5\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/7fb4546bd76e7146?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/7fb4546bd76e7146?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2qaMC8f22GtAtnuMT-0slH\">\r\n      IRT with covariates\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Phil Chalmers &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>rphilip....@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 08:02PM -0500\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Hi Bo,<br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; in the model without covariates, I assume that it is the residual variance<br>\r\n&gt; that is fixed to one. If that&#39;s the case, is there a way to convert these<br>\r\n&gt; parameters to the same metric so that we can compare them?<br>\r\n <br>\r\nYes, and indeed for any model that doesn&#39;t freely estimate the variance of<br>\r\nthe latent trait you should consider changing the identification to the<br>\r\nversion where the latent variable scale is determined by an item (say, item<br>\r\n1) by freeing the latent trait variance parameter and setting the slope of<br>\r\nthe identification item to 1. This is actually the default in most SEM<br>\r\nsoftware, precisely for this reason.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nBecause this is a simulation study just be careful about the scaling of the<br>\r\nitem parameters and traits. I often will just generate data given that the<br>\r\nfirst item slopes is always fixed at 1, and change the latent variance and<br>\r\nremaining parameters through the simulations. HTH.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nPhil<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_6\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/ff8c3143a446e339?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/ff8c3143a446e339?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1P4DA_hWf_DRaK6Op34fjI\">\r\n      EAP score estimation for multiple groups\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Pedro Martelleto &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>martelle...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 05:49AM -0800\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Thank you Phil, your answer helped a lot.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_group_thread_7\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/c4b4008a0a7e2fab?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/t/c4b4008a0a7e2fab?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IvmJd_nQ0QQkRYHSQHORC\">\r\n      Using MIRT results for SEM\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Felix Fischer &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>drhans...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Mar 06 03:51AM -0800\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Hi,<br>\r\n <br>\r\na measurement model within a SEM and an IRT model is basically the same. if <br>\r\nyou have an established IRT measurement model, you can use it to estimate <br>\r\nscores and then use these scores in a path model. the downside is that than <br>\r\nyour model assumes the latent scores to be true, ignoring their (known) <br>\r\nerror. there are ways to incorporate that as well, eg by imputing plausible <br>\r\nvalues. another approach would be to run a latent regression in mirt and <br>\r\nfixing the itemparameters to your values before. or you could reestimate <br>\r\nthe measurement parameters within a SEM. that might make the most sense if <br>\r\nyou&#39;re not entirely sure whether results of your pilot study are robust.<br>\r\n <br>\r\ni think there are many roads to go here and each have pros and cons - <br>\r\ndepends a lot on your study.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nbest, felix<br>\r\nOn Saturday, March 6, 2021 at 6:05:06 AM UTC+1 Bo wrote:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_8000448611954619043_m_8675005890025881190_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:5px 20px\">\r\n  <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:#636363;font-size:11px\">\r\n      \r\n      You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to updates for this group. You can change your settings on the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/mirt-package/join\" style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/mirt-package/join&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471803347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ly5P7pwAoFCYNKINDEUqv\">group membership page</a>.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it send an email to <a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>mirt-package...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr></tbody>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
    ]
